    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62723,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 136,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "<p>Uterus, fallopian tube, ovary, and rarely in the peritoneum {11781521; 19543245; 21337036; 156063; 19133002}</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-17T14:41:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62724,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 136,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "<p>These tumours are usually asymptomatic and incidentally discovered during surgeries for other conditions; however, they can present as a mass or be detected in endometrial curettings {11781521; 21337036}. Uterine tumours can be associated with immunosuppression, which is seen more commonly with large or multifocal/diffuse tumours in this site {19396001; 29148537; 30099776}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-21T18:36:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62725,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 136,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "<p>Adenomatoid tumour is an uncommon neoplasm {11781521; 21337036}, and its occurrence in the peritoneum is even rarer {19133002; 156063}. The median ages of patients with uterine and fallopian tube tumours, respectively, are 44&nbsp;years and 56&nbsp;years {21337036}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-17T14:41:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62726,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 136,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:09:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62727,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 136,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "<p>Adenomatoid tumours are genetically defined by somatic missense mutations in the <em>TRAF7</em> gene {29148537}, similar to well-differentiated papillary mesothelial tumours {30171198}. Adenomatoid tumours demonstrate intact/retained nuclear expression of BAP1 and uniformly lack <em>BAP1</em>, <em>CDKN2A</em>, and <em>NF2</em> mutations or deletions that characterize the majority of mesotheliomas {29148537; 27813512}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-17T14:42:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62728,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 136,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "<p>Tubal tumours may measure up to 1&ndash;2&nbsp;cm and are subserosal. Most uterine tumours are located in the outer myometrium; they are usually solitary, &lt;&nbsp;4&nbsp;cm, and solid but rarely can be diffuse, multicentric, multifocal, large (up to 11&nbsp;cm), or cystic {12959144; 11781521; 21337036}. Regardless of site of origin, most tumours have relatively ill-defined borders and a nodular, greyish-white, firm cut surface {11781521}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-17T14:46:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62729,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 136,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>These tumours show a variable combination of slit-like, tubular, or cystic branching spaces and solid areas intermixed with smooth muscle bundles. The neoplastic cells are eosinophilic and cuboidal or flattened, with mild to moderate atypia. Short papillae are seen in grossly cystic tumours. Usually, there are thread-like bridging strands within the luminal spaces. Signet-ring cells, vacuolated lipoblast-like cells, and a lymphoid infiltrate may be seen. Immunohistochemistry is not necessary for the diagnosis, but tumour cells express calretinin, WT1, D2-40, cytokeratin AE1/AE3, and CAM5.2 {11781521; 19543245; 21337036}. Adenomatoid tumours of the genital tract uniformly have intact/retained nuclear expression of BAP1, in contrast to mesothelioma, which frequently demonstrates loss of nuclear BAP1 expression {29148537; 27813512; 27067777}. These tumours should be differentiated from leiomyoma, adenocarcinoma, well-differentiated papillary mesothelial tumour, peritoneal inclusion cysts, and mesothelioma with adenomatoid-like areas {21337036}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-17T14:48:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62730,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 136,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:09:16"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
